<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - CANTV started.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - CANTV started.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Caspian Securities said on Thursday it had started coverage of Venezuelan telephone company Compania Nacional Telefonos de Venezuela, or CANTV, with a rating of buy.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Our 12-month price target of $35 per (American Depositary Share) implies potential total returns of 23 percent,&quot; analysts Joanne Showalter and Tony Figueiredo wrote in a report.</p>
<p>-- &quot;... CANTV trades at a 54 percent discount to the Latin telco average. We believe CANTV should trade at a premium to Brazilian telcos, similar to the more mature telcos in Mexico, Argentina and Chile.&quot;</p>
<p>-- CANTV shares were up 1/2 to 29-1/8 in New York trade.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
</text>
